        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
